  "body": "## Summary\nThe `validatePrice()` function in `UniswapPriceOracle` incorrectly calculates the time-weighted average price (TWAP), resulting in the derivation always being zero. This renders the slippage protection mechanism completely ineffective, allowing any trade to pass validation regardless of price manipulation.\n\n## Finding Description\nThe `validatePrice()` function is designed to protect against price manipulation by comparing the current spot price against a TWAP with a configurable slippage tolerance. However, the TWAP calculation contains a flaw:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 cumulativePrice = cumulativePriceLast + (tradePrice * elapsedTime);\nuint256 timeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime;\n```\n\nSubstituting the first equation into the second:\n```\ntimeWeightedAverage = ((cumulativePriceLast + tradePrice * elapsedTime) - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime\n                    = (tradePrice * elapsedTime) / elapsedTime\n                    = tradePrice\n```\n\nSince `timeWeightedAverage` always equals `tradePrice`, the derivation calculation on line 82 will always produce zero:\n```solidity\nuint256 derivation = (tradePrice > timeWeightedAverage)\n    ? ((tradePrice - timeWeightedAverage) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage\n    : ((timeWeightedAverage - tradePrice) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage;\n```\n\nWith `derivation = 0`, the validation `derivation <= slippage` (line 86) will always return `true`, regardless of the actual price deviation.\n\nI recommend reading this article and going towards the `Only calculating the last 1 hour TWAP in Solidity` section as there is a code example of how this should be implemented: https://rareskills.io/post/twap-uniswap-v2\n\n## Impact Explanation\nThis vulnerability completely bypasses the oracle's slippage protection mechanism.\n\nAn attacker can manipulate the spot price through flash loans or large trades, and `validatePrice()` will still return `true`, allowing the manipulated price to be accepted.\n\n## Likelihood Explanation\nThis issue will occur every time `validatePrice()` is called.\n\n## Recommendation\nStore historical cumulative price observations to calculate a proper TWAP. Implement something like this:\n\nAdd `lastCumulativePrice` state variables\nCalculates TWAP from stored vs current cumulative prices\n\n```solidity\n    /// @dev Validates the current price against stored TWAP.\n    function validatePrice(uint256 slippage) external view returns (bool) {\n        require(slippage <= maxSlippage, \"Slippage overflow\");\n\n        // Fetch current cumulative price\n        uint256 currentCumulativePrice;\n        if (direction == 0) {\n            currentCumulativePrice = IUniswapV2(pair).price1CumulativeLast();\n        } else {\n            currentCumulativePrice = IUniswapV2(pair).price0CumulativeLast();\n        }\n\n        // Require at least one block since last update\n        if (block.timestamp == lastUpdateTimestamp) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        \n        uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - lastUpdateTimestamp;\n        uint256 tradePrice = getPrice();\n\n        // Calculate TWAP using stored historical observation\n        uint256 timeWeightedAverage = (currentCumulativePrice - lastCumulativePrice) / elapsedTime;\n\n        // Calculate derivation percentage\n        uint256 derivation = (tradePrice > timeWeightedAverage)\n            ? ((tradePrice - timeWeightedAverage) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage\n            : ((timeWeightedAverage - tradePrice) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage;\n\n        return derivation <= slippage;\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## PoC\nAdd this test in autonolas-tokenomics/test:\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.28;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {UniswapPriceOracle} from \"../contracts/oracles/UniswapPriceOracle.sol\";\n\n/// @dev Mock Uniswap V2 Pair\ncontract MockUniswapV2Pair {\n    address public token0;\n    uint112 private reserve0;\n    uint112 private reserve1;\n    uint32 private blockTimestampLast;\n    uint256 public price0CumulativeLast = 1e24;\n    uint256 public price1CumulativeLast = 1e23;\n    \n    constructor(address _token0, address /* _token1 */) {\n        token0 = _token0;\n    }\n    \n    function setReserves(uint112 _reserve0, uint112 _reserve1) external {\n        reserve0 = _reserve0;\n        reserve1 = _reserve1;\n        blockTimestampLast = uint32(block.timestamp);\n    }\n    \n    function getReserves() external view returns (uint112, uint112, uint32) {\n        return (reserve0, reserve1, blockTimestampLast);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract UniswapPriceOracleTest is Test {\n    UniswapPriceOracle public oracle;\n    MockUniswapV2Pair public pair;\n    \n    address constant NATIVE = address(0x1);\n    address constant OLAS = address(0x2);\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        pair = new MockUniswapV2Pair(NATIVE, OLAS);\n        pair.setReserves(1000e18, 10000e18); // Price: 10 OLAS per NATIVE\n        oracle = new UniswapPriceOracle(NATIVE, 100, address(pair)); // 1% max slippage\n    }\n    \n    /// @notice validatePrice() accepts ANY price manipulation\n    function testValidatePriceIssue() public {        \n        skip(13);\n\n        uint256 price1 = oracle.getPrice();\n        bool validPrice1 = oracle.validatePrice(1);\n        console.log(\"Initial price:    \", price1);\n\n        // Double the price (100% increase)\n        pair.setReserves(1000e18, 20000e18);\n\n        skip(13);\n        \n        uint256 price2 = oracle.getPrice();\n        bool validPrice2 = oracle.validatePrice(1);\n        console.log(\"Manipulated price:\", price2);\n        console.log(\"Price change:      %\", (price2 * 100) / price1 - 100);\n        console.log(\"Validation passes:\", validPrice1);\n        console.log(\"Validation passes:\", validPrice2);\n    }\n}\n```\nTest output:\n```text\n  Initial price:     10000000000000000000\n  Manipulated price: 20000000000000000000\n  Price change:      % 100\n  Validation passes: true\n  Validation passes: true\n```",
